# What must never reach the build context (rockysurf-ftl9.4).
#
# Two jobs. The obvious one is size — `node_modules` and the legacy AWS trees are most of the
# checkout and none of them are wanted in the image. The one worth stating is SECRETS: a
# developer's `.env`, `rockysurf.config.yaml` or `~/.rockysurf` copy sitting in the working
# tree would otherwise be baked into a layer and shipped to whoever pulls the image. The
# container gets its config from the entrypoint instead (see docker/entrypoint.sh).

# Installed and generated
**/node_modules
**/dist
packages/core/public
.pnpm-store

# Local secrets and state — never in an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
rockysurf.config.yaml
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
**/secret.key

# The legacy AWS-serverless implementation, kept as a port source only
backend
frontend
infrastructure

# The throwaway spike: its own workspace, its own lockfile, not a member
spike

# Repo tooling and history that the runtime has no use for
.git
.github
.beads
.claude
.codex
.agents
.plan
*.log
rockysurf-graph.html
